## DBsubject(Chemistry)
## DBchapter(Gases)
## DBsection(Kinetic Molecular Theory)
## Level(2)
## KEYWORDS('gases', 'pressure', 'temperature', 'particle behavior')
## Author('Stephanie Bryan')
## Institution(PCC)
## Language(en-US)

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    "PGstandard.pl",
    "PGML.pl",
    "parserPopUp.pl",
    "PGcourse.pl"
);

TEXT(beginproblem());

############################################################
# Images
############################################################

$sampleAImage = image(
    "SampleA.png",
    width    => 300,
    height   => 300,
    tex_size => 500,
    extra_html_tags =>
        'alt="Sample A: eight gas particles moving inside a container."'
);

$comparisonImage = image(
    "HigherT.png",
    width    => 300,
    height   => 300,
    tex_size => 500,
    extra_html_tags =>
        'alt="Eight gas particles moving faster inside a container of the same size as Sample A."'
);

############################################################
# Answers
############################################################

@temperatureEvidenceChoices = (
    "Choose...",
    "The arrows are longer, showing that the particles have a greater average speed.",
    "There are more particles in the container.",
    "The particles are closer together.",
    "The container is larger."
);

$temperatureEvidenceAnswer = PopUp(
    ~~@temperatureEvidenceChoices,
    "The arrows are longer, showing that the particles have a greater average speed."
);

@pressureChoices = (
    "Choose...",
    "increases",
    "decreases",
    "stays the same"
);

$pressureAnswer = PopUp(
    ~~@pressureChoices,
    "increases"
);

@reasonChoices = (
    "Choose...",
    "The particles collide with the walls more frequently and exert more force during each collision.",
    "The particles collide with the walls less frequently and exert less force during each collision.",
    "There are fewer particles available to collide with the walls.",
    "The frequency and force of the particle-wall collisions do not change."
);

$reasonAnswer = PopUp(
    ~~@reasonChoices,
    "The particles collide with the walls more frequently and exert more force during each collision."
);

############################################################
# Problem
############################################################

BEGIN_PGML

##Changing the temperature of a gas

Gas pressure results from collisions between gas particles and the
walls of their container.

In each particle diagram:

* each circle represents one gas particle;
* each arrow shows the direction and relative speed of a particle; and
* a longer arrow represents a greater particle speed.

### Initial state:

[@ $sampleAImage @]*

### New state:

[@ $comparisonImage @]*

How do you know that the temperature is higher in the new state?

[@ $temperatureEvidenceAnswer->menu() @]*

Compared with the initial state, the pressure in the new state [@ $pressureAnswer->menu() @]*.

Which statement best explains this pressure change?

[@ $reasonAnswer->menu() @]*

END_PGML

ANS($temperatureEvidenceAnswer->cmp());
ANS($pressureAnswer->cmp());
ANS($reasonAnswer->cmp());

############################################################
# Solution
############################################################

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

The temperature is higher because the arrows are longer, showing that
the particles have a greater average speed. Temperature is related to
the average kinetic energy of the gas particles.

The pressure **increases**.

The faster particles reach and collide with the container walls more
frequently. Each collision also produces a greater change in momentum,
so the particles exert a greater force on the walls.

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();